    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2016-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We can factor a \\(9!\\) out of the numerator and simplify. \\[\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{9!(11 \\cdot 10 - 10)}{9!} &=11 \\cdot 10 - 10 \\\\&= 110 - 10 \\\\&= 100. \\end{aligned}\\] Thus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(10!\\) or \\(9!\\) from the numerator",
        "Use \\(11!=11\\cdot10\\cdot9!\\)"
      ],
